From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] Raise the rolling-summary profiles' summary output cap

The two Gemini 3.8 Flash high rolling-summary profiles
(google-gemini-3-8-flash-high-rolling-summary and its notes-off
variant) took the Provider Adapter's summary_max_output_tokens of
8,192. At thinking_level high the model's thinking counts against that
cap, so on thinking-heavy games a summary request can spend it before
writing any text. Four empty summaries in a row end the run with
AGENT_ERROR ("Harness summary compaction failed to produce a
completed, non-empty summary after 4 response failures"). Both
profiles now set summary_max_output_tokens to 65,536, the
max_output_tokens of every action request. Nothing else changes: the
175,000-token trigger, the 8,192-token input headroom,
MAX_CONTEXT_LENGTH and the summary prompts are as before, and the
Standard and Provider Adapter profiles are unchanged (the Provider
Adapter keeps 8,192). Configuration validation still holds:
175,000 + 65,536 + 8,192 is below the 1,048,576 context capacity.

Tests: the rolling-summary profile equals Standard with the Provider
Adapter's compaction policy except the summary cap, which equals the
action output budget; both agents' compactors use 65,536; the S1/S2
summary request snapshots carry max_output_tokens 65,536 while the
Provider Adapter's keep 8,192; and the notes-off = Provider Adapter
parity checks (one and two compactions, a buffered GAME_OVER frame,
overflow recovery, an unparseable reply) allow exactly that difference
in summary requests and no other.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
